### Maplenou Customer Service API — manual test collection
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client) and JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Prerequisite: the stack runs with the demo profile (docker compose up -d) — see docs/guide/backend-processing.md.
# Click "Send Request" above each block, from top to bottom: tokens are captured and reused.
# Postman: import backend/http/postman/*.json (same steps, with automatic checks). Swagger UI: /swagger-ui.html.

@api = http://localhost:8081
@jean = 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111
@sophie = 44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444444
@amina = 66666666-6666-4666-8666-666666666666

### 0. Health (public)
GET {{api}}/actuator/health

### 1. Demo personas (demo profile only)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/dev/users

### 2. Token for Jean K. (customer)
# @name jeanLogin
POST {{api}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{jean}}" }

### 3. Token for Sophie N. (support agent)
# @name sophieLogin
POST {{api}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{sophie}}" }

### 4. Token for Amina K. (support manager)
# @name aminaLogin
POST {{api}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{amina}}" }

### 5. Active categories (cached; returns an ETag — resend with If-None-Match to get 304)
# @name categories
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5b. Same request revalidated: 304 Not Modified, no body
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
If-None-Match: {{categories.response.headers.ETag}}

### 6. Jean's orders and deliveries (ecosystem context, demo adapter)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/me/references
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Jean creates a ticket
# @name created
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Colis non reçu",
  "description": "Ma commande est marquée livrée mais je n'ai rien reçu.",
  "categoryCode": "DELIVERY",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "urgent": false
}

### 8. Jean tries the Critical priority -> 422 CRITICAL_PRIORITY_RESERVED (BR-036)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subject": "Test", "description": "Test", "categoryCode": "OTHER", "priority": "CRITICAL" }

### 9. Sophie sees the queue (open tickets, newest first)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets?open=true&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 10. Sophie takes the ticket (agentId null = assign to me)
PUT {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{created.response.body.id}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 11. Sophie writes an internal note (never visible to Jean)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{created.response.body.id}}/internal-notes
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Appeler le livreur avant 16 h.", "clientMessageId": "note-1" }

### 12. Sophie replies to Jean (first response: SLA first-response target met)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{created.response.body.id}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Bonjour Jean, nous vérifions auprès du livreur.", "clientMessageId": "reply-1" }

### 13. Ecosystem context of the ticket (order, payment, delivery) — support only
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{created.response.body.id}}/context
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 14. Jean reads his ticket: no internal note, no SLA data (BR-014)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{created.response.body.id}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 15. Jean's notifications (AGENT_REPLIED…) with ticketNumber/detail for English rendering
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/notifications?size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 16. Sophie resolves the ticket
PUT {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{created.response.body.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "RESOLVED", "comment": "Colis retrouvé et livré." }

### 17. Jean asks to reopen
# @name reopen
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{created.response.body.id}}/reopen-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Le colis livré n'est pas le mien." }

### 18. Sophie approves (ticket back to IN_PROGRESS, new resolution SLA period)
PUT {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{created.response.body.id}}/reopen-requests/{{reopen.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "APPROVE", "note": "Nous reprenons la demande." }

### 19. Full history (append-only audit)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{created.response.body.id}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 20. Manager dashboard and report
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{aminaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/reports/summary?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31
Authorization: Bearer {{aminaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 21. Jean cannot open the back-office dashboard -> 403
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 22. Push channel of the server ("firebase" or "log-only") and Jean's registered devices
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/notifications/push-status
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 23. Register a device token (a fake one is enough to test the API; real ones come from Firebase)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/notifications/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "http-client-test-token", "platform": "WEB" }

### 24. Send Jean a test push now (log-only mode: written to the backend log)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/notifications/devices/test
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 25. Unregister the device
DELETE {{api}}/api/v1/support/notifications/devices/http-client-test-token
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 26. SLA clock mode (always = 24/7, weekends and holidays count — default)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/admin/sla-settings
Authorization: Bearer {{aminaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 27. Sign in with a Maplenou account (only with MAPLENOU_LOGIN_ENABLED=true and Bakend running)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/auth/maplenou/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phoneNumber": "+22890000000", "password": "your-password" }

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- iteration 6 (UPGRADE-PLAN items)

### 28. Vocabulary: statuses (with their kind), manual transitions and priorities — every client
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/vocabulary
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 29. Jean opens a ticket about an order
# @name orderTicket
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "subject": "Produit cassé", "description": "Le vase est arrivé cassé.", "categoryCode": "RETURN_REFUND", "orderRef": "CMD-2026-0456" }

### 30. Sophie takes it, then inserts a canned reply
PUT {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{orderTicket.response.body.id}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{}

### 31. Canned replies
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/canned-replies
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 32. Ask Maplenou to open a return for Jean (ECOSYSTEM_MODE=demo answers without calling Bakend)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{orderTicket.response.body.id}}/actions/refund-request
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "reason": "Produit reçu cassé, photo dans le ticket.", "productCondition": "DAMAGED" }

### 33. Waiting for the customer: the resolution clock pauses (sla.pausedSince)
PUT {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{orderTicket.response.body.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "status": "WAITING_FOR_CUSTOMER", "comment": "Photo du colis ?" }

### 34. AI help status, suggestion decision, reply draft (needs AI_ASSIST_ENABLED=true and the assistant)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/ai/status
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{orderTicket.response.body.id}}/ai/draft-reply
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "language": "fr" }

### 35. Resolve, then Jean rates the answer (1 to 5, once)
PUT {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{orderTicket.response.body.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{sophieLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "status": "RESOLVED", "comment": "Retour ouvert chez le vendeur." }

###
POST {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/{{orderTicket.response.body.id}}/satisfaction
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jeanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "rating": 5, "comment": "Merci !" }

### 36. CSV export of the open tickets (managers and administrators)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/tickets/export.csv?open=true&lang=fr
Authorization: Bearer {{aminaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 37. SLA targets per priority
GET {{api}}/api/v1/support/admin/sla-policies
Authorization: Bearer {{aminaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 38. Prometheus metrics (METRICS_TOKEN in .env; 404 when it is empty)
GET {{api}}/actuator/prometheus
Authorization: Bearer local-metrics-token-0123456789
